<node name="CPTS Prep Notes" unique_id="1" master_id="0" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="1" foreground="#af65f4" ts_creation="1792540800" ts_lastsave="1792540800">
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h1" weight="heavy" foreground="#af65f4">CPTS Prep Notes</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>Certified Penetration Testing Specialist. This file holds your methodology, module notes and exam workspace as a tree of nodes. Pick a node on the left to open it.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy" foreground="#af65f4">The exam
</rich_text>
<rich_text>CPTS is a 10-day black-box engagement against an enterprise-like Active Directory network: external foothold, pivot inside, move laterally and work toward Domain Admin across Windows and Linux hosts. 14 flags, about 12 needed to pass.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>Four parts:</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy" link="node 2" foreground="#af65f4">Methodology</rich_text>
<rich_text>: your methodology, as numbered blank phases that you name and fill in your own way.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy" link="node 13" foreground="#af65f4">Modules</rich_text>
<rich_text>: your notes, one per Academy module, in course order. Your methodology links back to these.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy" link="node 540" foreground="#af65f4">Exam</rich_text>
<rich_text>: your exam workspace, with targets, credentials, findings, flags and a log for each day, laid out like the report.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy" link="webs https://cnmoseman.github.io/htb-study-trackers/cpts/tracker/" foreground="#af65f4">CPTS Study Tracker</rich_text>
<rich_text>: the day-by-day study plan for this cert. Check off tasks there as you go.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy" foreground="#d9822b">Read this first
</rich_text>
<rich_text>Flags alone do not pass you. The commercial-grade report is pass/fail on its own, and people who pass often hand in 100-150 pages with an executive summary, attack narrative and CVSS-rated findings.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy" foreground="#2f9e44">Do the reporting module
</rich_text>
<rich_text>Don't leave </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 513" foreground="#af65f4">M27 - Documentation &amp; Reporting</rich_text>
<rich_text> for last. It shows you how to take notes during an engagement and turn them into the kind of report HTB grades.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#af65f4">How to use it</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>1. Work through the course in order. As you finish each module, fill in its note.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>2. Build your methodology as you go. Rename each </rich_text>
<rich_text family="monospace" foreground="#af65f4">Fill in</rich_text>
<rich_text> phase to a step in your own workflow, and add or delete phases as you need. For a new phase, duplicate </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Templates › Methodology Phase</rich_text>
<rich_text> (</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Tree › Duplicate Node</rich_text>
<rich_text>) and drag the copy under </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Methodology</rich_text>
<rich_text>.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>3. Fill each phase with your own checklist, commands and decision points, and link back to the module notes: select some text, pick </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Insert › Insert/Edit Link</rich_text>
<rich_text>, choose </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">To Node</rich_text>
<rich_text> and pick the note.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>4. Keep one node per tool and one per service under </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Tools &amp; Services</rich_text>
<rich_text>. For a new one, duplicate </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Templates › Tool</rich_text>
<rich_text> or </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Templates › Service</rich_text>
<rich_text> (</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Tree › Duplicate Node</rich_text>
<rich_text>) and drag the copy under </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Tools &amp; Services</rich_text>
<rich_text>. </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 538" foreground="#af65f4">Nmap</rich_text>
<rich_text> and </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 539" foreground="#af65f4">SMB</rich_text>
<rich_text> are there to start you off. Link them from your module notes and phases so the commands you use most are one click away.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>5. Each module has one child node per Academy section. Expand a module in the tree to see its sections.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>6. On exam day, start at </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 540" foreground="#af65f4">Exam</rich_text>
<rich_text> and work from your methodology. The main nodes are in the </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Bookmarks</rich_text>
<rich_text> menu. Click any link to jump to the node behind it.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
